IMPLEMENTED CONTRACT
- Frozen Python 3.8-compatible dataclasses (manual __slots__) for condition definitions, evidence, condition/group traces, expressions, named groups, and compiled plans.
- Stable NewType IDs for policy, condition, group, and producer; independent classification and required/optional/ignored mode enums.
- Instance-scoped ProducerRegistry.bind(...) stores immutable tuple bindings; duplicate and unknown keys are typed errors; there is no singleton or global registry.
- compile_policy(...) accepts an already-parsed mapping only. It does not accept a path and imports no YAML/ROS/filesystem/network modules.
- The sole root must be explicit `all`. Required leaves occur once as direct root members. Optional leaves occur once below exactly one all/any/quorum subtree. Ignored leaves stay outside root for later trace evaluation.
- Named expression references resolve explicitly; unknown condition/group/producer IDs, cycles, duplicate/unreachable leaves, invalid quorum bounds, malformed timing, and callable/import-path producer values are typed compilation errors.
- No implicit prerequisite graph or second gate was introduced.

